welcome back to cbs mornings the lion  state of queen elizabeth continues in  london her children and grandchildren  will stand watch tonight while mourners  file past the coffin the line stretching  from westminster hall is estimated five  miles long this morning a few hours ago  officials stopped people from joining  the line saying it was completely full  holly williams is watching the  preparations for monday's funeral  good morning well the united kingdom has  plenty of experience organizing  elaborate public events  from the funeral of princess diana to  royal weddings all require meticulous  preparation but this is reportedly the  most complex security operation london's  ever seen with around 10 000 police  officers and 1500 military personnel  already deployed the queen's funeral  will be held here at westminster abbey  in the heart of london filled with  historic buildings and narrow streets  the abbey sits just across the road from  the british houses of parliament just  down the road from the prime minister's  residence number 10 downing street and a  stone's throw from london's crowded  shopping and entertainment district the  west end that's where two police  officers were stabbed and hospitalized  just this morning the mayor said it was  not terrorism related  president biden and dr jill biden will  attend the funeral along with many of  the crowned heads of europe the japanese  emperor and of course the uk's own royal  family  one british official likened the  logistics of the queen's funeral to  organizing a hundred state visits all at  the same time  nate  that was holly williams in london thank  you gail and norah o'donnell will lead  our coverage of queen elizabeth funeral  on monday morning starting at 5 30  eastern time looking forward to that
 

